01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Hamnet  is a 2025 biographical historical tragedy film directed by Chloé Zhao, who co-wrote
the screenplay with Maggie O'Farrell, based on the 2020 novel by O'Farrell.

11
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
The film dramatises the family life of William Shakespeare and his wife Anne
Hathaway as they cope with the death of their 11-year-old son Hamnet.

12
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
It stars Jessie Buckley and Paul Mescal as Agnes and William, alongside
Emily Watson, Joe Alwyn, and Noah Jupe in supporting roles.

13
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
Hamnet had its world premiere at the 52nd Telluride Film Festival on 29 August 2025 and received a
limited theatrical release by Focus Features in the United States and Canada on 26 November.

14
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
It received a wide theatrical release on 5 December and was released by
Universal Pictures in the United Kingdom on 9 January 2026.

15
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
The film received critical acclaim, with the performances of
Buckley and Mescal receiving particular praise.

16
01:36:00,000 --> 01:36:06,000
It was listed among the top ten films of 2025 by the American Film Institute.

17
01:42:00,000 --> 01:42:06,000
The film won Best Motion Picture – Drama and Best Actress in a Motion Picture – Drama (for Buckley) at the 83rd
Golden Globe Awards, and Buckley additionally won the Critics’ Choice Award for Best Actress.

18
01:48:00,000 --> 01:48:06,000
The film received eight nominations at the 98th Academy Awards, including Best
Picture, Best Director for Zhao and Best Actress for Buckley.

